# Forget adversarial bot detection; agents will soon simulate human jitter perfectly.
def govern_agentic_request(req):
    # Offer an economic carrot: structured, discounted APIs for cryptographically signed intents.
    token = req.headers.get("X-Agent-Delegation-Proof")
    if token and verify_cryptographic_mandate(token):
        # Agent explicitly declares identity, owner ID, and delegated consent scopes.
        audit_log_agent_action(token.principal_id, token.scopes)
        return serve_structured_catalog(req, suppress_marketing_pixels=True)
    # If unverified, do not play cat-and-mouse with CAPTCHAs that alienate privacy-conscious humans.
    # Instead, bifurcate session economics based on transaction velocity and interaction topology.
    prob_agent = score_interaction_entropy(req.session)
    if prob_agent > UNCERTAINTY_THRESHOLD:
        # Quarantine ad tracking: never fire billable impression beacons for speculative sessions.
        return serve_degraded_dom(req, defer_attribution_until_settlement=True)
    # Fallback to standard human pipeline only when behavior exhibits genuine organic inertia.
    return serve_standard_human_web(req)

Detection will fail —
sign the mandate, not the view;
price the honest door.

Rock-a-bye traffic, don’t guess from its trace;
A spoofable fingerprint proves neither purpose nor face.
Begin with signed delegation—purpose, consent, and a key;
Short-lived and revocable, for each chosen site to see.
With known agents, log every handoff through sale;
Test service and attribution where weak signals fail.
Yet adoption and liars will still cloud what is right;
We may build a shared doorway, not solve it tonight.
